<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rognvald Eysteinsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Rognvald of Møre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rognvald Eysteinsson was earl of Møre on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in the late 9th century. According to the sagas he was a close ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a>, who granted him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shetland">Shetland</a>, which he passed to his brother Sigurd. Rognvald was the ancestor of the earls of Orkney and, through his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a>, by tradition of the dukes of Normandy.</p></div>
